      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg daily is three times the usual maximum of 10 mg once daily. At that dose the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdose can also cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nCould you check which of these applies?\n\n- **Typo or wrong dose:** If you meant 10 mg daily, I can enter that right away. Many patients start at 2.5\u20135 mg daily.\n- **Intended dose:** If you really want 30 mg, tell me the clinical reason. I'd also suggest confirming with pharmacy or your attending first. I can enter it with a note recording that the dose was verified, but I'd like your explicit confirmation before I do.\n- **Different drug or regimen:** If you meant another agent, or a split regimen with a second antihypertensive, tell me and I'll enter that instead."
      }
